// 0.0.3 V06 std library: `io` module — console and standard input.
//
// The functions in this module are implemented by the VM (`exec_builtin`,
// fleen-vm/src/vm.rs), not in Fleen source (D8): they need capabilities the
// language cannot express — standard input and formatted line output. Their
// names live only in the compiler's builtin table and are bound by the
// resolver from the module path, so this file carries only documentation.
//
//     import std.io;
//     std.io.println("hi");     // print + trailing newline
//     line = std.io.read_line(); // read one line of stdin (without the \n)
//
// `std.io.print` is the prelude `print` (same builtin, same variadic
// `(string...) -> unit` signature): the resolver routes the qualified
// spelling to the bare-name builtin so `std.io.print(...)` works after
// `import std.io;` just like the unqualified `print(...)`.

// `print` prints each argument (unconditionally string-typed) with no
// trailing newline. Prelude spelling: usable without any import. VM
// intrinsic `print` (same as `std.io.print`).

// `println` prints each argument (unconditionally string-typed, like
// `print`) followed by a newline. VM intrinsic `std.io.println`.

// `read_line` reads one line from standard input, without its trailing
// newline. Returns an empty string at end of input. VM intrinsic
// `std.io.read_line`.
// 0.0.4 T06: `std.io.sleep(n)` — awaitable timer. Inside an async body the
// compiler lowers the call to `Call std.io.sleep; Suspend`, so the task parks
// until `n` milliseconds elapse (the VM records the deadline and the executor
// wakes it). A synchronous caller of `sleep` gets a no-op (no `Suspend` is
// emitted). Returns `unit` after the delay.
